# {{ project_slug }}

{{ project_description }}. Made from [python-backend-template](https://github.com/7331/python-backend-template).
`BACKEND-API.md` holds the rules the code follows, and `AGENTS.md` holds the rules for agents and pull requests.

## Run it

```sh
cp .env.example .env
{%- if include_postgres %}
cp .env.database-owner.example .env.database-owner
{%- endif %}
docker compose up -d --build --wait
curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
```

For day-to-day work, `BACKEND-API.md` (Local development) has two loops that need no image rebuild: compose watch,
and the backend on the host with `serve-api --reload`.

## Env files

- `.env` is read by the API. Fill in every key that `.env.example` leaves empty.
{%- if include_postgres %}
- `.env.database-owner` holds the Postgres superuser password. Only the `postgres` and `migrate` containers read it.
- `deploy/postgres/backup.env.example` lists the WAL-G backup keys for production.
{%- endif %}

None of them is committed. Production keeps them outside the checkout with mode 600.

## Checks

```sh
uvx prek run --stage pre-push --all-files
```

That runs every gate, and `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs the same command on every pull request and on `main`. Git
runs the fast gates on commit, the rest on push, and checks the commit subject against the PR title rule. The e2e
flows in `e2e/` run by hand when a change needs one and are never a CI or hook gate.

## First push

Run these once, in this order. The ruleset comes last because it refuses a direct push to `main`.

1. Commit and push `main`:

   ```sh
   git add --all
   git commit --message "chore: start from python-backend-template"
   gh repo create {{ project_slug }} --private --source . --push
   ```

2. Create the labels. An issue form's label that does not exist is not applied, and GitHub says nothing.

   ```sh
   gh label create bug --force --color d73a4a --description "Something doesn't work as intended"
   gh label create enhancement --force --color a2eeef --description "New behaviour, or a refactor, cleanup, tooling, docs or performance change"
   gh label create question --force --color d876e3 --description "Needs an owner decision before work starts"
   gh label create idea --force --color c5def5 --description "Kept for later, not work yet"
   gh label create parked --force --color ededed --description "Skipped for now by the owner, to be picked up later"
   gh label create security --force --color b60205 --description "Touches authentication, keys, encryption or privacy"
   gh label create priority:urgent --force --color b60205 --description "Users blocked, or data or security at risk now: drop everything"
   gh label create priority:high --force --color d93f0b --description "A broken flow with no workaround: next up"
   gh label create priority:low --force --color c2e0c6 --description "Polish, fine if it never happens"
   ```

3. Allow only squash merges, and turn on auto-merge and branch deletion on merge:

   ```sh
   gh api --method PATCH "repos/{owner}/{repo}" \
     --field allow_squash_merge=true --field allow_merge_commit=false --field allow_rebase_merge=false \
     --field allow_auto_merge=true --field delete_branch_on_merge=true \
     --field squash_merge_commit_title=PR_TITLE --field squash_merge_commit_message=PR_BODY
   ```

4. Turn on Dependabot alerts and security updates. They read `uv.lock` and open a pull request the day an advisory
   lands. `.github/dependabot.yml` covers the monthly version updates.

   ```sh
   gh api --method PUT "repos/{owner}/{repo}/vulnerability-alerts"
   gh api --method PUT "repos/{owner}/{repo}/automated-security-fixes"
   ```

5. Protect `main`: no deletion, no force push, a pull request for every change, the `Check` and `Conventional title`
   checks on a branch that is up to date, squash only.

   ```sh
   gh api --method POST "repos/{owner}/{repo}/rulesets" --input .github/rulesets/main.json
   ```

CI runs on GitHub's `ubuntu-latest`. To move it to a self-hosted runner, set the repository variable `CI_RUNNER` to
the runner's labels as JSON: `gh variable set CI_RUNNER --body '["self-hosted","<label>"]'`.

`.github/workflows/image-scan.yml` builds the backend image every Monday and fails on a fixable HIGH or CRITICAL
vulnerability. When an OS package is the cause, move `APT_EPOCH` in `backend/Dockerfile` to today's date so the next
build upgrades it. It is the only scheduled workflow. Delete the file to stop it.

## Deploy

On the host, with the env files outside the checkout:

```sh
export {{ environment_prefix }}_ENVIRONMENT_FILE=<deploy .env>
{%- if include_postgres %}
export {{ environment_prefix }}_DATABASE_OWNER_ENVIRONMENT_FILE=<database owner env file>
export {{ environment_prefix }}_POSTGRES_BACKUP_ENVIRONMENT_FILE=<backup env file>
{%- endif %}
deploy/deploy.sh
```

It builds the image from the checkout, starts the stack behind the reverse proxy{% if include_postgres %}, and takes a base backup{% endif %}.
{%- if include_postgres %}
Once per host, install the backup schedule's systemd unit (`BACKEND-API.md`, Backup schedule). Until it runs,
`deploy/deploy.sh` deploys, warns and exits 1.
{%- endif %}

## Update from the template

```sh
uvx copier update --trust
```

The tree must be clean. Copier applies what changed in the template since the version in `.copier-answers.yml` and
leaves conflicts as inline markers. It never overwrites this file or `AGENTS.md`. Each
[release](https://github.com/7331/python-backend-template/releases) lists the steps an update needs by hand.
